<section class="how">
    <h2>How to Use the Date Calculator</h2>
    <p>There are two ways to use this tool. The first is adding or subtracting time from a specific date. Pick your starting date, choose whether you want to add or subtract, then enter the number of years, months, and days. Hit Calculate and the result shows your target date along with the day of the week it falls on.</p>
    <p>This is useful for figuring out deadlines, contract end dates, subscription expirations, or counting down to events. If you have a 90-day return window starting from January 5th, for example, you add 90 days and get the exact cutoff date.</p>
    <p>All calculations run locally in your browser. No data is sent anywhere.</p>
</section>

<section class="formula">
    <h2>How the Date Math Works</h2>
    <p>Adding days to a date is straightforward arithmetic on the underlying day count. Months are trickier because they have different lengths. Adding one month to January 31st has to land on the last day of February since February 28th or 29th is the furthest that month goes.</p>
    <p>Leap years matter here too. A year is a leap year if it is divisible by 4, except that century years must be divisible by 400. So 2000 was a leap year but 1900 was not. This calculator handles all of those edge cases automatically, including Feb 29 birthdays.</p>
    <p>Business day calculations skip Saturdays and Sundays. If your deadline lands on a weekend the actual last working day is the Friday before.</p>
</section>

<section class="examples">
    <h2>Common Date Calculation Examples</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>90-day warranty period:</strong> Product purchased on March 1, 2025. Add 90 days. Warranty expires May 30, 2025.</li>
        <li><strong>6-month lease:</strong> Lease starts on February 1, 2025. Add 6 months. Lease ends August 1, 2025.</li>
        <li><strong>Days between dates:</strong> Need to know how many days between July 4 and Thanksgiving (November 27)? Enter both dates and the calculator returns 146 days.</li>
        <li><strong>Legal 30-day notice:</strong> Notice served on October 15, 2025. Add 30 days. Effective date is November 14, 2025.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

